# https://github.com/halo-box/strix-llama.cpp.git @ same commit. That
# lazy-tensor feature generalized the old
#     if (use_mmap) { ... }
# gate in `load_all_data()` to
#     const bool from_mapping = use_mmap || lazy.has(cur);
#     if (from_mapping) { ... }
# so that lazy-read tensors (which always require a mapping, per the
# TENSOR_READ_LAZY comment "requires mmap for now" in
# llama-model-loader.h) are read from the mmap the same way full-mmap
# tensors are, even when `use_mmap` is otherwise false for the invocation.
